    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1965-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Completing the square gives \\[y=(x-4)^2+c-16.\\] The vertex is \\((4,c-16),\\) so it lies on the \\(x\\)-axis when \\(c=16.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
